# R1.4.6 hydration. `dev-state/` is the dev profile's live-ish store root (the
# ONLY writable mount of mist-backend-dev); `data/hydration-snapshots/` holds
# the versioned artifacts snapshot.py dumps out of it. Both are regenerable --
# dev-state by restore, the artifacts by a hydration run -- and both contain
# SQLite/vault state that must never enter git history.
dev-state/
data/hydration-snapshots/

# Live-path smoke test. `smoke-state/` is the throwaway stack's scratch root and
# the ONLY writable mount of mist-backend-smoke. It holds a real event store, a
# real vault and real conversation content produced by the smoke run, and the
# runbook deletes it at teardown. It must never enter git history, and it must
# never be picked up by a `git add -A` run mid-experiment.
smoke-state/
